From 337cbc1c5344bb6b23f0f80c3a5c7ec8c59ed10e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 06:50:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Fix three faults found in a live run
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Only one slide reached READY. The slide content model is a nine-branch
discriminated union, which becomes a top-level oneOf in JSON Schema, and
Gemini's structured output does not handle that reliably — the title slide
uses the simplest branch and succeeded while the rest failed validation
twice and were marked ERROR. The model is now asked for a flat draft: one
object, a type enum, and a uniform blocks array, which is a quarter the
schema size and contains no union. That draft is narrowed to typed content
in code, where a shortfall degrades to a simpler layout instead of failing
the slide. Verified across seven drafts including a data slide with no
figures, a one-step process and a single-column comparison: all three
awkward cases fall back to a concept slide and render clean.

PDF references were silently ignored. pdf-parse v2 removed its default
export in favour of a PDFParse class, so extractPdfText threw on every PDF
and the error was swallowed, which is why a PPTX reference worked and a PDF
did not. Extraction now uses the v2 API, and unreadable files are reported
rather than discarded — including a file that yields no text at all, which
previously looked identical to a successful read of nothing. Verified
against the uploaded documents: 80,227 characters recovered from the PDF
that had been producing nothing.

Reopening a draft course showed no slides. The course endpoint never
returned slides or sections, so the editor rebuilt each lesson from an
undefined array, and the preview map is only populated during generation,
leaving the preview button with nothing to show. The endpoint now returns
both, and the editor restores the preview state from stored HTML.

